==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[take]] [[back]]|takes back|taking back|took back|taken back}}

# To [[retract]] an [[earlier]] [[statement]]
#: {{usex|lang=en|No, you are not fat; I '''take''' it all '''back'''.}}
# To [[cause]] to [[remember]] some [[past]] [[event]] or [[time]]
#: {{usex|lang=en|That tune '''takes''' me '''back''' to my childhood.}}
# To [[resume]] a [[relationship]]
#: {{usex|lang=en|She has forgiven him, and '''taken''' him '''back'''.}}
# To [[regain]] [[possession]] of something
#: {{usex|lang=en|The wedding is off, and he has '''taken back''' the ring.}}
# To [[return]] something
#: {{usex|lang=en|'''Take back''' faulty goods to the shop where you bought them.}}

